    "summary": "Model completed and passing all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nROOT CAUSE OF THE FAILURE: the accepted decision girder.Ec was 32500 MPa, which is the C50 modulus of the superseded JTG D62-2004 table. Per JTG 3362-2018 Table 3.1.5 (node JTG3362-3.1.5) C50 concrete has Ec = 3.45e4 MPa = 34500 MPa. The too-low modulus made the model ~3% too flexible, giving f1 = 5.4104 Hz instead of 5.5734 Hz. This propagated: the impact factor lane.mu had also been computed from the wrong frequency, so the L2-2 check (impact factor consistent with the model's first vertical frequency) failed. The KG reported no suspect decisions, so I localized the error by re-proposing each accepted decision against its governing formula.\n\nREPAIRS:\n1. girder.Ec revised 32500 -> 34500 MPa (evidence JTG3362-3.1.5).\n2. Re-ran modal analysis: f1 = 5.5734 Hz (stable).\n3. lane.mu recomputed from JTGD60-4.3.2 with f1 = 5.5734 Hz: mu = 0.1767*ln(f1) - 0.0157 = 0.28787.\n\nMODEL SUMMARY (spine_beam_2d, continuous, 3 spans 20+25+20 m = 65 m):\n- Girder: 4 precast prestressed small-box girders, C50, Ec = 34500 MPa, gamma = 26 kN/m3; single midspan section A = 1.0605 m2, I = 0.25166 m4; combined A = 4.2421 m2, I = 1.00663 m4; w = 110.294 kN/m, m = 11.243 t/m (girder self-weight only).\n- Bearings (two per girder end, 8 per support line, 300x350 mm, 4 layers x 8 mm): Abutment 0 / Pier 2 / Abutment 3 - PTFE sliding (Kv = 1.133e7 kN/m, Kh = 0, longitudinally free); Pier 1 - plain laminated elastomeric (Kv = 1.133e7 kN/m, Kh = 26250 kN/m, longitudinally spring = fixed point). S = 10.096.\n- Live load: Highway Class I, one-way, 3 design lanes, xi = 0.78, qk = 10.5 kN/m, Pk = 300/310/300 kN for spans 1/2/3.\n\nKEY RESULTS:\n- First vertical frequency f1 = 5.5734 Hz; impact factor mu = 0.2879.\n- Self-weight support reactions (kN): 820.49, 2764.07, 2764.07, 820.49; sum = 7169.1 kN = gamma*A*L, satisfying L3-1/L3-2.\n- Self-weight midspan moments: 2690.2 / 2967.7 / 2690.2 kNm; pier support moments -5649.0 kNm.